Protecting critical infrastructure from 25LSO-0163, 1.0
foreign adversaries.
FISCAL NOTE
This bill contains an appropriation of $209,800 from the GENERAL FUND to the
Office of Homeland Security. This appropriation is effective immediately.
This bill contains an authorization of up to 2 full-time positions.
DETAIL OF APPROPRIATION
Agency #: 001A Agency Name: Office of Homeland Security
Unit: (new) Critical Infrastructure
EXPENDITURE BY SERIES AND YEAR FY 2025 FY 2026 FY 2027
0100 Personnel/Benefit Costs $0 $209,800 $0
Total Expenditure Per Year: $0 $209,800 $0
Grand Total Expenditure: $209,800
Total Appropriated to Agency: $209,800
Total Appropriated by Fund:
GENERAL FUND $209,800
Description of appropriation:
The appropriation will be utilized to hire 2 additional critical infrastructure
protection personnel.
The fiscal impact to the Attorney General’s Office, Division of Criminal
Investigation (DCI) in indeterminable. The DCI does not know the volume of
investigations that may come from The Wyoming Office of Homeland Security (WOHS).
The DCI cannot estimate the number of investigations, the length of time for
those investigations, nor the resources that will be required.
NOTICE-AGENCY ESTIMATE OF ADMINISTRATIVE IMPACT REQUESTED
This bill has administrative impact that appears to increase duties or
responsibilities of one or more state agencies and may impact agency spending or
staffing requirements.
The following state agencies will be asked to provide their estimate of the
administrative fiscal impact prior to the first committee meeting held to
consider the bill:
Office of Homeland Security
